  <div class="corner-mark">
    Dialecta
    <span class="mark-rule"></span>
    <span class="mark-sub">MMXXVI</span>
  </div>
  <div class="parchment-inner">
    <span class="eyebrow">Why this exists</span>
    <h2 class="display">Most platforms reward<br>the <em>wrong thing.</em></h2>
    <p class="body">
      The loudest voice wins. The most outraged post spreads furthest. Certainty is
      rewarded; nuance is penalized. You&rsquo;ve felt the pull toward simpler, sharper,
      angrier. That pull isn&rsquo;t your weakness. It&rsquo;s the system working exactly as designed.
    </p>
    <p class="body">
      <strong>Dialecta is built on a different design.</strong> The mechanics that
      elsewhere reward reflexive anger and tribal conformity are here reoriented
      toward something else: curiosity, honest engagement, and the kind of thinking
      that only happens when you slow down enough to actually think.
    </p>
    <div class="callout">
      <p>The question isn&rsquo;t whether social media influences us. It&rsquo;s how much we&rsquo;re willing to be shaped by it without noticing.</p>
      <p class="attribution">From the essay that started this</p>
    </div>
    <p class="body">
      This platform isn&rsquo;t neutral. It&rsquo;s <strong>actively trying to make you a
      clearer thinker</strong>, not by telling you what to think, but by showing
      you how you think, and giving you the tools to do it better.
    </p>
<div class="section-mark"><span class="section-mark-num">§ III · The Classification</span></div>
<span class="eyebrow">The classification system</span>
    <h2 class="display">Every voice finds<br>its <em>place.</em></h2>
    <p class="body">
      Comments are never hidden. They&rsquo;re sorted into visible tiers based on what
      they&rsquo;re doing, not what they believe. Strong disagreement belongs in The Forum.
      Vague outrage lives in The Heat. The system doesn&rsquo;t silence you. It describes
      you, and invites you to say more.
    </p>
    <div class="tier-list">
      <div class="tier-row tier-forum">
        <div class="tier-row-icon"><svg class="tier-svg" width="28" height="28" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M3 7 L12 3 L21 7"/><line x1="2" y1="7.5" x2="22" y2="7.5" stroke-width="2.2"/><line x1="6" y1="9" x2="6" y2="19"/><line x1="12" y1="9" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="18" y1="9" x2="18" y2="19"/><line x1="3" y1="20" x2="21" y2="20" stroke-width="2.2"/></svg></div>
        <div>
          <span class="tier-row-kicker">Tier I</span>
          <h3 class="tier-row-name">The Forum</h3>
          <p class="tier-row-desc">Constructive, specific, fact-referenced or clearly reasoned. Strong disagreement belongs here, if it&rsquo;s about something specific.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="tier-row tier-spark">
        <div class="tier-row-icon"><svg class="tier-svg" width="28" height="28" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="0.5" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M13 2 L4 14 L11 14 L10 22 L20 9 L13 9 Z"/></svg></div>
        <div>
          <span class="tier-row-kicker">Tier II</span>
          <h3 class="tier-row-name">The Spark</h3>
          <p class="tier-row-desc">A genuinely interesting idea, but underdeveloped. The seed of something good. Invites expansion rather than resolution.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="tier-row tier-echo">
        <div class="tier-row-icon"><svg class="tier-svg" width="28" height="28" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M4 12 a8 8 0 0 1 14 -5"/><path d="M18 3 L18 7 L14 7"/><path d="M20 12 a8 8 0 0 1 -14 5"/><path d="M6 21 L6 17 L10 17"/></svg></div>
        <div>
          <span class="tier-row-kicker">Tier III</span>
          <h3 class="tier-row-name">The Echo</h3>
          <p class="tier-row-desc">Restates the article or a prior comment without adding to it. Not harmful, just not propulsive.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="tier-row tier-fog">
        <div class="tier-row-icon"><svg class="tier-svg" width="28" height="28" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="0.5" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M6.5 18 C 3.5 18, 2 16, 2 13.5 C 2 11, 4 9.5, 6 9.8 C 6.5 6.5, 9 5, 11.5 5 C 14.5 5, 16.5 7, 17 9.5 C 19.5 9.5, 22 11, 22 14 C 22 16.5, 20 18, 17.5 18 Z"/></svg></div>
        <div>
          <span class="tier-row-kicker">Tier IV</span>
          <h3 class="tier-row-name">The Fog</h3>
          <p class="tier-row-desc">Vague, unclear, or disconnected. The reader can&rsquo;t tell what the person believes or what point they&rsquo;re making.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="tier-row tier-heat">
        <div class="tier-row-icon"><svg class="tier-svg" width="28" height="28" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="0.5" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 2 C 10 6, 7 8, 7 13 C 7 17.5, 9.5 21, 12.5 21 C 16 21, 18 17.8, 17.8 14.5 C 17.6 12, 15.8 10, 14 9 C 14.5 11, 13.5 12, 12.5 11.5 C 12 9, 13 6, 12 2 Z"/></svg></div>
        <div>
          <span class="tier-row-kicker">Tier V</span>
          <h3 class="tier-row-name">The Heat</h3>
          <p class="tier-row-desc">Emotionally charged without constructive specificity. The argument is often in there. It just hasn&rsquo;t been separated from the feeling yet.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="tier-row tier-stance">
        <div class="tier-row-icon"><svg class="tier-svg" width="28" height="28" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="0.5" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-linecap="round"><line x1="6" y1="3" x2="6" y2="21" stroke-width="2.8"/><path d="M6 4 L18 8 L6 12 Z"/><line x1="3" y1="21" x2="9" y2="21" stroke-width="2.8"/></svg></div>
        <div>
          <span class="tier-row-kicker">Tier VI</span>
          <h3 class="tier-row-name">The Stance</h3>
          <p class="tier-row-desc">Heavy rhetoric, tribal framing, or coded language signaling team membership over idea engagement. More flag-planting than thinking.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="tier-row tier-breach">
        <div class="tier-row-icon"><svg class="tier-svg" width="28" height="28" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M9 7 a3 3 0 0 0 -3 3 v2 a3 3 0 0 0 3 3 h1"/><path d="M15 17 a3 3 0 0 0 3 -3 v-2 a3 3 0 0 0 -3 -3 h-1"/><line x1="3" y1="3" x2="21" y2="21" stroke-width="3"/></svg></div>
        <div>
          <span class="tier-row-kicker">Tier VII</span>
          <h3 class="tier-row-name">The Breach</h3>
          <p class="tier-row-desc">Name-calling, slander, targeted personal attacks. Suppressed from default view, not deleted, with the reason shown transparently.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
<div class="section-mark"><span class="section-mark-num">§ IV · The Process</span></div>
<span class="eyebrow">The process</span>
    <h2 class="display">How your words find<br>their <em>tier.</em></h2>
    <p class="body">
      Classification isn&rsquo;t done to you. You participate in it, alongside an AI
      engine and the community around you. Every stage is transparent. Every
      decision is contestable.
    </p>
    <div class="stage-list">
      <div class="stage">
        <div class="stage-num">I</div>
        <div>
          <div class="stage-title">You write freely</div>
          <div class="stage-body">No template, no prompt. Write what you actually think, the way you actually think it.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="stage">
        <div class="stage-num">II</div>
        <div>
          <div class="stage-title">The engine reflects</div>
          <div class="stage-body">Before you post, an AI reads your submission, not to judge it but to describe what it&rsquo;s doing. It identifies your <strong>core claim</strong>, detects rhetorical patterns, and suggests a tier with a plain-language reason. It names the <strong>strongest element in your writing</strong> first.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="stage">
        <div class="stage-num">II.5</div>
        <div>
          <div class="stage-title">You respond to the reflection</div>
          <div class="stage-body">You can <strong>amend</strong> your submission, <strong>respond for the record</strong>, or <strong>post as-is</strong>. None of these choices are wrong. Your response, if reasoned, carries weight in the final classification.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="stage">
        <div class="stage-num">III</div>
        <div>
          <div class="stage-title">The community engages</div>
          <div class="stage-body">Readers can nominate your post for reclassification, up or down, and must give a reason. Their nominations are visible. The system is always contestable.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
<div class="section-mark"><span class="section-mark-num">§ V · The Wait Architecture</span></div>
<span class="eyebrow">The wait architecture</span>
    <h2 class="display">Slowness is<br>a <em>feature.</em></h2>
    <p class="body">
      Every timer in this system is the platform saying: <strong>this thought is
      worth sitting with.</strong> The waits are disclosed, not hidden. They are
      not friction. They are ritual. The moment the platform makes your post
      permanent is designed to feel earned.
    </p>
    <p class="body">
      Once your post hardens, it&rsquo;s yours permanently. You can append to it at any
      time. Your additions are visible and tracked. Public refinement of your
      thinking is treated here as a strength, not a liability.
    </p>
    <div class="wait-grid">
      <div class="wait-row"><div class="wait-label">After writing, before AI analysis appears</div><div class="wait-time">8 sec</div></div>
      <div class="wait-row"><div class="wait-label">After AI analysis, before Stage 2.5 options activate</div><div class="wait-time">12 sec</div></div>
      <div class="wait-row"><div class="wait-label">Full comment reflection window</div><div class="wait-time">30 min</div></div>
      <div class="wait-row"><div class="wait-label">Article submission reflection window</div><div class="wait-time">24 hrs</div></div>
      <div class="wait-row"><div class="wait-label">Community reclassification nomination</div><div class="wait-time">20 sec</div></div>
    </div>
    {{!-- The "Path A vs Path B" reflect-first / reflection-mode choice
          used to live as a callout here and as a selector in the
          Commitment section (§ VIII). Removed 2026-04-29: the choice
          confused new members during sign-on. The options are now
          surfaced where they actually apply, in the post composer. --}}
<div class="section-mark"><span class="section-mark-num">§ VI · The Deeper Purpose</span></div>
<span class="eyebrow">The deeper purpose</span>
    <h2 class="display">This platform is trying<br>to <em>grow you.</em></h2>
    <p class="body">
      The tier system isn&rsquo;t the point. The point is what happens when you engage
      with it over time. Every AI reflection that names a pattern in your thinking
      is a chance to see something about yourself that most environments never show you.
    </p>
    <p class="body">
      When the engine detects a pattern, <strong>emotional frontloading, tribal
      reflex, certainty performance</strong>, it names it, explains why it
      happens, and links you to a short, honest explainer. One pattern per
      submission. Always framed as human, never as deficiency.
    </p>
    <div class="growth-grid">
      <div class="growth-card"><div class="growth-tag">Pattern</div><div class="growth-card-title">Emotional Frontloading</div><div class="growth-card-sub">Leading with feeling rather than claim. The argument is in there. It just hasn&rsquo;t been separated from the emotion carrying it.</div></div>
      <div class="growth-card"><div class="growth-tag">Pattern</div><div class="growth-card-title">Tribal Reflex</div><div class="growth-card-sub">Evaluating arguments by who is making them, not what they contain. Agreement or disagreement before engagement.</div></div>
      <div class="growth-card"><div class="growth-tag">Pattern</div><div class="growth-card-title">Certainty Performance</div><div class="growth-card-sub">Expressing more confidence than the evidence warrants, because uncertainty reads as weakness in social environments.</div></div>
      <div class="growth-card"><div class="growth-tag">Pattern</div><div class="growth-card-title">False Binary</div><div class="growth-card-sub">Collapsing a spectrum into a choice. Team A or Team B, when the reality lives in the space between.</div></div>
    </div>
    <p class="body" style="margin-top: 32px;">
      Your private profile tracks which patterns have appeared in your writing over
      time, not as a score, not as a judgment, but as a <strong>personal map of
      your own tendencies.</strong> The goal isn&rsquo;t to correct you. It&rsquo;s to make
      you more legible to yourself.
    </p>
<div class="section-mark"><span class="section-mark-num">§ VII · Learn by Doing</span></div>
<span class="eyebrow">Learn by doing</span>
    <h2 class="display">Can you read<br>the <em>tier?</em></h2>
    <p class="quiz-intro">Before you commit, try classifying three real comments. This is the fastest way to understand what the system actually sees, and what it misses.</p>

